/T (1. INTRODUCTION )
/E (1. INTRODUCTION )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
221 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (Loan approval is an important process in the banking and financial sector because financial institutions must carefully evaluate applicants before granting loans. The decision to approve or reject a loan is usually based on several demographic, financial and social factors such as income level, education, credit history, employment status and property area. Accurate loan approval decisions are essential for reducing financial risk and ensuring that loans are provided to eligible applicants.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
222 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (The dataset used in this study was obtained from Kaggle and it represent loan application records from Dream Housing Finance, a housing finance company that provides home loans to customers across urban, semi-urban and rural areas. Customers first apply for a home loan, after which the company evaluates their eligibility before making approval decisions. Traditional loan approval processes are often manual, time-consuming and may sometimes lead to inconsistent or biased decisions. As the number of loan applications increases, there is a growing need for automated and data-driven decision-making systems.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (Machine learning techniques provide an effective solution for improving loan approval prediction. By analyzing historical applicant data, machine learning models can identify important patterns and relationships that influence loan approval decisions. These models can support financial institutions by improving prediction accuracy, reducing manual effort, increasing consistency and supporting faster decision-making.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (This study focuses on developing a machine learning-based system to predict loan approval status using applicant information. Several supervised machine learning models were developed and compared to identify the most suitable model for loan approval prediction. The study also aims to identify the most important variables influencing loan eligibility through feature importance analysis.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (Objectives of the study:)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (The main objective of this study is to develop a machine learning model capable of accurately predicting loan approval status. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (The specific objectives include identifying the most important variables influencing loan eligibility, evaluating model performance using accuracy and other classification metrics, as well as improving the efficiency and consistency of the loan approval process.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (This study is significant because it demonstrates the practical application of machine learning techniques in banking and financial systems. And also it can help to automate the loan approval process, reduce manual workload, support better financial risk management and assist institutions in making more consistent and reliable lending decisions.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
