/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (A recent study by Velvigneswar, J., & Kumari, P. S. \(2025\). Loan approval prediction using machine learning. International Journal of Advanced Research in Computer and Communication Engineering, 14\(7\). developed a machine learning-based loan approval prediction system using algorithms such as Logistic Regression, Random Forest, Decision Tree and SVM. The study applied preprocessing techniques including missing value imputation, encoding, feature scaling and SMOTE for class balancing. The results showed that SVM achieved the best overall performance among the evaluated models with an accuracy of 79.67%, while others achieved comparatively lower performance levels. However, despite applying SMOTE for balancing the dataset, the achieved accuracy values remained lower compared to several recent studies. The research mainly focused on prediction performance and provided limited discussion regarding detailed model adequacy testing and interpretability analysis.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (Another related study by Jadhav, A., et al. \(2023\). Loan approval prediction using machine learning. International Research Journal of Modernization in Engineering Technology and Science, 5\(5\).investigated loan approval prediction using several machine learning algorithms, including Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, Random Forest and Gradient Boosting. The study used applicant demographic and financial information to predict loan approval status. Their results showed that Logistic Regression achieved the highest prediction accuracy of 80%, outperforming the other evaluated models. However, the authors also noted that prediction performance heavily depends on the quality and quantity of available data. In addition, the study mainly focused on accuracy-based evaluation and provided limited discussion regarding feature importance analysis and detailed model validation techniques.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (Overall, previous studies show that machine learning is effective for loan approval prediction. However, many of them used only a few models, focused mainly on accuracy or had limited interpretability analysis.Some studies also used balancing techniques such as SMOTE or undersampling without fully examining whether class imbalance significantly affected model performance.Therefore, this study compares multiple machine learning models using evaluation metrics such as Accuracy, F1-Score and ROC-AUC and also includes feature importance analysis to identify key factors influencing loan approval decisions)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
