/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (Multiple machine learning models were evaluated to identify the most suitable algorithm for loan approval prediction. Five supervised machine learning models were developed and evaluated to predict loan approval status using applicant demographic, financial and social information. The models used in this study were Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting and Support Vector Machine \(SVM\). Hyperparameter tuning was performed using GridSearchCV to identify the optimal parameter combinations for each model.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
438 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (The primary objective of these models was to classify whether a loan application would be approved \(Loan_Status = Y\) or rejected \(Loan_Status = N\). Model performance was evaluated using Accuracy, F1-Score, ROC-AUC score, Confusion Matrix, Classification Report and Feature Importance Analysis. These evaluation metrics provided a comprehensive understanding of model performance and predictive capability.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
