522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (The main objective of this study was to identify the important factors affecting loan approval and to develop a machine learning model capable of predicting loan approval status accurately. Based on the results obtained from exploratory data analysis, preprocessing, model development and evaluation, the objectives of the study were successfully achieved.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
523 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 951 0 R
/E (The exploratory data analysis \(EDA\) helped identify several meaningful relationships within the dataset. Variables such as Credit_History, Education, Married, Property_Area and income-related features showed noticeable effects on loan approval decisions. In particular, applicants with valid credit histories had a much higher chance of receiving loan approval compared to applicants without valid credit histories.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
524 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 952 0 R
/E (Several machine learning models were evaluated, including Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting and Support Vector Machine \(SVM\). Among these models, Logistic Regression showed the best overall performance with strong Accuracy, F1-Score and ROC-AUC results. Although Decision Tree achieved a similar accuracy value, Logistic Regression demonstrated better classification balance and more reliable prediction capability.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
525 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 953 0 R
/E (The model evaluation results further confirmed the effectiveness of the selected model. The classification report, confusion matrix and ROC curve analysis showed that the Logistic Regression model was able to predict loan approval status accurately and reliably.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
526 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 954 0 R
/E (Feature importance analysis revealed that Credit_History was the most influential variable affecting loan approval decisions. Other important variables included Property_Area_Semiurban, Married, Education and CoapplicantIncome. These findings are consistent with real banking practices, where financial reliability and applicant background are important in loan approval decisions.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
527 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 955 0 R
/E (An important strength of the study was the consistency between the EDA findings and the advanced machine learning analysis. The patterns observed during EDA were further supported by the feature importance analysis and model results, increasing the reliability of the study findings.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
528 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 956 0 R
/E (The dataset had a slight class imbalance, with about 68.7% approved loan applications. Since the imbalance was not severe, techniques such as SMOTE or undersampling were not used. The selected model still achieved good performance, indicating that the imbalance did not significantly affect model reliability. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
529 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 957 0 R
/E (Hyperparameter tuning using GridSearchCV also contributed to improving model performance and stability by identifying the most suitable parameter combinations for each algorithm. This allowed a fair comparison among models and improved the reliability of the final results.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
